<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>C6.S1 — Matrix elements and cost of the QFT</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<div style="background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:5px solid #026573;border-radius:8px;padding:16px 22px;margin-bottom:14px;"><p style="color:#026573;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0;">C6.S1 — The transform itself</p></div><p>Let \(n={@n@}\), \(N=2^{n}\) and \(F_N|j\rangle=\frac{1}{\sqrt N}\sum_k e^{2\pi ijk/N}|k\rangle\).</p><p>(a) Give the matrix element \(\langle k|F_N|j\rangle\) for general \(j,k,N\) (use <code>j</code>, <code>k</code>, <code>N</code>).</p><p>\(\langle k|F_N|j\rangle=\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p><p>(b) Give the number of controlled-rotation gates in the standard QFT circuit on \(n\) qubits, as a function of <code>n</code>.</p><p>gates \(=\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]</p><p>(c) Evaluate that count for \(n={@n@}\).</p><p>value \(=\) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) Directly from the definition, \(\langle k|F_N|j\rangle=e^{2\pi ijk/N}/\sqrt N\).</p><p>(b) Qubit \(\ell\) receives one Hadamard and controlled rotations from every later qubit, giving \(\sum_{\ell=1}^{n}(n-\ell)=\binom{n}{2}=\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\).</p><p>(c) For \(n={@n@}\) this is \({@ta3@}\).</p><p>Compare the classical FFT at \(\Theta(N\log N)=\Theta(n2^{n})\): the quantum circuit is exponentially smaller, but it transforms amplitudes, which cannot be read out directly. Truncating rotations below \(2\pi/2^{O(\log(n/\varepsilon))}\) yields the approximate QFT with only \(O(n\log(n/\varepsilon))\) gates.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1000000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber></idnumber>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2024010100</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text>n : rand_with_step(4,9,1);
ta1 : exp(2*%pi*%i*j*k/N)/sqrt(N);
ta2 : n*(n-1)/2;
ta3 : n*(n-1)/2;</text>
    </questionvariables>
