  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>C6.S3 — Ancilla count and success probability of QPE</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<div style="background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:5px solid #026573;border-radius:8px;padding:16px 22px;margin-bottom:14px;"><p style="color:#026573;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0;">C6.S3 — Sizing the register</p></div><p>(a) Give the guaranteed lower bound on the probability that \(t\)-qubit phase estimation returns the nearest \(t\)-bit approximation of \(\varphi\) (an exact expression).</p><p>\(p_{\min}=\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p><p>(b) Give the number of ancillas \(t\) needed for \(n\) bits of precision with failure probability at most \(\varepsilon\) (use <code>n</code> and <code>eps</code>; you may use <code>ceiling</code>).</p><p>\(t=\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]</p><p>(c) Evaluate it for \(n={@nn@}\) and \(\varepsilon=1/100\).</p><p>\(t=\) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) The geometric-sum amplitude at the nearest integer satisfies \(|\alpha_b|^{2}\ge 4/\pi^{2}\approx0.405\), independently of \(t\) and \(\varphi\).</p><p>(b) Bounding the tail of the Fejér kernel gives \(t=n+\left\lceil\log_2\left(2+\frac{1}{2\varepsilon}\right)\right\rceil\).</p><p>(c) With \(n={@nn@}\), \(\varepsilon=1/100\): \(\lceil\log_2 52\rceil=6\), so \(t={@nn@}+6={@ta3@}\).</p><p>Alternatively, repeat the \(t=n\) circuit \(O(\log(1/\varepsilon))\) times and take the median — the standard powering trick, cheaper in qubits but more expensive in circuit repetitions.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
